<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-19">19 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Black Prince captures King John II at Poitiers</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a>'s outnumbered army defeated the French at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> II. His huge ransom and the chaos that followed brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to the brink of collapse.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poitiers-1356" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-poitiers-1356.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poitiers-1356">Battle of Poitiers (1356)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Poitiers was fought on 19 September 1356 near Poitiers in western France during the Hundred Years' War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-scheut">Battle of Scheut</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Scheut was fought on 17 August 1356 at Scheut, near Anderlecht west of Brussels, during the War of the Brabantine Succession.</p></div></li></ol></section>
